  "_comment": [
    "Tabs and sub-chips for the products/ page. products/index.html and sync_catalog.py (via categories.py) both read this file; keep the matching rules simple enough that both agree.",
    "How a product is placed: (1) ids in 'hidden' are left off the page entirely (their detail pages stay live); (2) an id in 'overrides' goes straight to that 'tab' or 'tab/sub'; (3) Fan Gear if fan_gear matches (see below); (4) otherwise the tab from item_types[item_type].",
    "Within the tab, the sub is the first sub (in match_order, else display order) whose keywords appear in the name as whole words, case-insensitive; else item_types[item_type].sub; else no sub (the product still shows under the tab's All chip).",
    "Fan Gear = officially licensed only: a licensed_keywords match, OR a licensed_brands match together with a team name, OR an id in fan_gear.include. A team name on its own never qualifies (sync_catalog.py warns so someone can decide). fan_gear.exclude keeps an id out.",
    "Every item_type in products.json must be listed in item_types, or sync_catalog.py fails CI."
  ],
